; A buildable area surveyed on the site grid, and five proposed footprints set
; out on the building's own grid.
;
; Nothing here says whether anything fits. That is read back out of the corners,
; the frames and the claims every time the question is asked: the footprints are
; carried into the site frame across the georeference, offset by whatever
; clearance is required of them, overlaid on the buildable area and measured.
;
; The five footprints are the situations a siting answer has to tell apart. One
; clears by metres, one clears by ten millimetres against an uncertainty of
; twenty, one crosses the boundary, one is not over the plot at all, and one has
; one is set out on a grid nobody stated the accuracy of the fit for — which is
; undecidable rather than either of the first two.

; The buildable area: thirty metres by twenty on the site grid, surveyed from
; the same control point the georeference was fitted against.
(vertex geom:V-01
  (label "Buildable area, south-west corner")
  (frame frame:site)
  (position
    (id survey:P-0001)
    (value (0.0 0.0 0.0) m)
    (source "Boundary survey BS-2026-011, Acme Surveys")
    (method method:total-station)
    (accuracy (independent 0.004 m) (systematic 0.008 m control:CP-1))
    (date "2026-03-11")))

